...RESPONDENTS (BY SRI.RANGEGOWDA N.R., ADV. FOR R1;
 SRI.JANARDHAN REDDY, ADV. FOR R2)
 THESE MFA'S

5 ORDER (i) Appeal filed by the owner of the bus is allowed;
 (ii) Appeal filed by the petitioner is  dismissed as having become  infructuous;
(iii) The impugned judgment and award is set aside;
(iv) The matter is remanded back to the Tribunal to the stage of filing of the objection statement of the owner of the bus;
(v) The Tribunal is requested to afford an opportunity to both the parties to lead additional evidence and to adjudicate the claim on merits in accordance with law;
(vi) As the accident is of the year 2011 and injury sustained by the petitioner, the Tribunal is requested to dispose of the - 13 - NC: 2024:KHC:38057 claim petition within 3 months from the date of first day of appearance of both the parties;
(vii) Without further notice, the parties shall appear before the Tribunal on 16.10.2024.
(viii) The owner of the bus shall deposit a sum of Rs.75,000/- on the first day of appearance before the Tribunal and Tribunal shall keep the said amount in interest earning FD.
SD/-
(T.G. SHIVASHANKARE GOWDA) JUDGE MKM Sri M P Thippeswamy vs Sri Thimmanna on 13 September, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/55677444/
